From: Multiview <operations+codex@aperim.com>
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/http: a closed chunked reply of unknown size ends with EOF

FFmpeg 9.0 (62006041cc, "don't return EOF unless we actually read all
bytes") returns EIO from http_read_stream() whenever the connection is gone
and s->off < s->filesize. For a chunked reply filesize is UINT64_MAX, so a
reply whose last chunk was received and whose connection was then closed
("Last chunk received, closing conn") is reported as an I/O error instead of
EOF. Seen on chunked 302 -> chunked 200 playlist redirects (jmp2.uk ->
pluto.tv). Only report EIO when the size is actually known. A sized reply
that is cut short still returns EIO.

Not fixed by upstream 5db1e097dc/ca5300c9f4 (requested_end() still yields
UINT64_MAX for chunked replies). Drop when the pin moves to a release that
handles this.
---
diff --git a/libavformat/http.c b/libavformat/http.c
index 35f886f..3b80b70 100644
--- a/libavformat/http.c
+++ b/libavformat/http.c
@@ -1838,8 +1838,10 @@ static int http_read_stream(URLContext *h, uint8_t *buf, int size)
     int reconnect_delay_total = 0;
     int conn_attempts = 1;
 
+    /* A chunked reply has no known size: once its last chunk closed the
+     * connection, the end of the data is a clean EOF, not a short read. */
     if (!s->hd)
-        return s->off < s->filesize ? AVERROR(EIO) : AVERROR_EOF;
+        return s->filesize != UINT64_MAX && s->off < s->filesize ? AVERROR(EIO) : AVERROR_EOF;
 
     if (s->end_chunked_post && !s->end_header) {
         err = http_read_header(h);
